**Root causes and fix summary:**

| Bug | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Overselling | `check_stock` → `charge` → `decrement` had a race window; two concurrent checkouts could both pass the stock check before either decremented | New `atomic_decrement(quantity)` holds an `asyncio.Lock` across the check-and-decrement, making it atomic |
| Ghost charges | If `charge` succeeded but `decrement` failed (or vice versa), inventory and charge records diverged | Reordered: decrement first (reserves the item), then charge. If charge fails, `increment` restores inventory — no partial state |

The lock ensures only one coroutine can be mid-decrement at a time, and the reordered flow means every successful charge corresponds to exactly one inventory decrement. No order is charged more than once.
